/* RMSC: the project's own service programs, for *PGM objects and test        */
/* programs to bind to.                                                       */
/*                                                                            */
/* TOBi's CRTBNDRPGFLAGS has no BNDDIR parameter, so anything binding to RMSC  */
/* must carry ctl-opt bnddir('RMSCPGM') in its source.                        */
/*                                                                            */
/* This used to add "and RUCRTRPG is not given one either". That is no longer */
/* true: IBM i Testing 1.3.4 passes bndDir and bndSrvPgm through to RUCRTRPG  */
/* from .vscode/testing.json. The ctl-opt route is kept anyway, and it is the */
/* right one here rather than merely the older one - testing.json applies     */
/* only when the EXTENSION compiles the suite, and tools/verify.sh compiles   */
/* all thirteen of them with RUCRTRPG directly from a shell. A testing.json   */
/* binding would pass in the Test Explorer and fail the verification.         */
/*                                                                            */
/* The entry is library-qualified (&O, not *LIBL) deliberately: an entry       */
/* recorded as *LIBL makes activation search the caller's library list,       */
/* which would put a library-list requirement on every job calling RMSC.      */
!DLTOBJ OBJ(&O/&N) OBJTYPE(*BNDDIR)
CRTBNDDIR BNDDIR(&O/&N) +
          TEXT('RMSC: own service programs')
ADDBNDDIRE BNDDIR(&O/&N) +
   OBJ( (&O/RMSC *SRVPGM) )
